s, the Lunarch enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on Mikaeus.\\n{T}, Remove a +1/+1 counter from Mikaeus: Put a +1/+1 counter on each other creature you control.', "Mugging deals 2 damage to target creature. That creature can't block this turn.", 'Other Dinosaurs you control get +1/+1.\\n{5}{G}: Create a 3/3 green Dinosaur creature token with trample.', 'Other Elf creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{T}: Add {G} for each Elf you control.', 'Outnumber deals damage to target creature equal to the number of creatures you control.', 'Pillar of Flame deals 2 damage to any target. If a creature dealt damage this way would die this turn, exile it instead.', 'Prevent all noncombat damage that would be dealt to you and creatures you control.\\nWhenever a nontoken creature enters the battlefield under your control, create a 2/2 white Unicorn creature token.', 'Prowess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)', 'Put a +1/+1 counter on each of up to two target creatures.', 'Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature, then put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature. That creature gains first strike until end of turn. You gain 2 life.', 'Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature. That creature gains reach until end of turn.', 'Put all creature cards from all graveyards onto the battlefield under your control.', 'Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control. You lose life equal to its mana value.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\n{1}{R}: Minotaur Sureshot gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "Reach\\nUlvenwald Hydra's power and toughness are each equal to the number of lands you control.\\nWhen Ulvenwald Hydra enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.", 'Reach\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Weaver of Lightning deals 1 damage to target creature an opponent controls.', "Return all creatures to their owners' hands except for Krakens, Leviathans, Octopuses, and Serpents.", "Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand. If it's a Zombie card, draw a card.", "Return target creature to its owner's hand. If that creature is attacking, you may put it on top of its owner's library instead.", "Return target creature to its owner's hand. Scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)", "Return target creature you control and target creature you don't control to their owners' hands.", "Return target nonland permanent to its owner's hand.\\nDraw a card.", 'Return up to two target creature cards from your graveyard to your hand, then discard a card.', 'Return up to two target creature cards from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Rupture Spire enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Rupture Spire enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you pay {1}.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'Sacrifice Ronom Unicorn: Destroy target enchantment.', 'Sacrifice a Beast: You gain 4 life.', "Sarkhan's Rage deals 5 damage to any target. If you control no Dragons, Sarkhan's Rage deals 2 damage to you.", 'Scrounging Bandar enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it.\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may move any number of +1/+1 counters from Scrounging Bandar onto another target creature.', 'Spitting Earth deals damage to target creature equal to the number of Mountains you control.', "Storm Sculptor can't be blocked.\\nWhen Storm Sculptor enters the battlefield, return a creature you control to its owner's hand.", "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nAt the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, that player sacrifices a creature.", 'Target creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'Target creature gets +1/+7 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +2/+2 and gains lifelink until end of turn. (Damage dealt by the creature also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', 'Target creature gets +2/+2 and gains trample until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn. You gain 1 life for each attacking creature you control.', 'Target creature gets +4/-4 until end of turn.', "Target creature gets +7/+7 and gains trample until end of turn. It must be blocked this turn if able. (A creature with trample can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", 'Target creature gets -3/-3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets -4/-0 until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'Target creature must be blocked this turn if able.\\nDraw a card.', "Target creature you control gains vigilance and trample until end of turn. It deals damage equal to its power to target creature you don't control.", "Target land you control becomes a 4/4 Elemental creature with haste until end of turn. It's still a land. It must be blocked this turn if able.", 'Target player mills two cards.\\nDraw a card.', 'Terrarion enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Terrarion: Add two mana in any combination of colors.\\nWhen Terrarion is put into a graveyard from the battlefield, draw a card.', "This spell can't be countered.\\nGreen spells you control can't be countered.\\n{4}{G}{G}: Until end of turn, each Elf creature you control has base power and toughness 5/5 and becomes a Dinosaur in addition to its other creature types.", "This spell can't be countered.\\nVolcanic Fallout deals 2 damage to each creature and each player.", 'This spell costs {1} less to cast for each instant and sorcery card in your graveyard.', 'This spell costs {1} less to cast if you control a Wizard.\\nCounter target spell.', 'This spell costs {1} less to cast if you control a creature with flying.\\nDraw two cards.', "This spell costs {2} less to cast if it targets a Dinosaur you control.\\nPut a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control. Then that creature fights target creature you don't control. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)", 'This spell costs {3} less to cast if a creature died this turn.\\nFlying, deathtouch', 'This spell costs {X} less to cast, where X is the total power of creatures you control.\\nTrample', 'Thriving Bluff enters the battlefield tapped.\\nAs Thriving Bluff enters the battlefield, choose a color other than red.\\n{T}: Add {R} or one mana of the chosen color.', 'Thriving Grove enters the battlefield tapped.\\nAs Thriving Grove enters the battlefield, choose a color other than green.\\n{T}: Add {G} or one mana of the chosen color.', 'Thriving Heath enters the battlefield tapped.\\nAs Thriving Heath enters the battlefield, choose a color other than white.\\n{T}: Add {W} or one mana of the chosen color.', 'Thriving Isle enters the battlefield tapped.\\nAs Thriving Isle enters the battlefield, choose a color other than blue.\\n{T}: Add {U} or one mana of the chosen color.', 'Thriving Moor enters the battlefield tapped.\\nAs Thriving Moor enters the battlefield, choose a color other than black.\\n{T}: Add {B} or one mana of the chosen color.', 'Towering Titan enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it, where X is the total toughness of other creatures you control.\\nSacrifice a creature with defender: All creatures gain trample until end of turn.', "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)\\nAt the beginning of each end step, if Inferno Hellion attacked or blocked this turn, its owner shuffles it into their library.", "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)\\nHaste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nAt the beginning of the end step, sacrifice Ball Lightning.", 'Trample\\nOther Minotaur creatures you control get +1/+1 and have trample.', 'Trample\\nWhenever Rampaging Brontodon attacks, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn for each land you control.', 'Trample\\nWhenever another nontoken creature enters the battlefield under your control, you may draw a card.', 'Up to two target creatures each get +1/+2 until end of turn. You gain 2 life.', 'Up to two target creatures each get +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Vigilance', "Vigilance (Attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.)", 'Vigilance\\n{2}: Add one mana of any color.', "When Affectionate Indrik enters the battlefield, you may have it fight target creature you don't control. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)", 'When Ambassador Oak enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 green Elf Warrior creature token.', "When Ancestral Statue enters the battlefield, return a nonland permanent you control to its owner's hand.", 'When Archaeomender enters the battlefield, return target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Armorcraft Judge enters the battlefield, draw a card for each creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it.', "When Awakener Druid enters the battlefield, target Forest becomes a 4/5 green Treefolk creature for as long as Awakener Druid remains on the battlefield. It's still a land.", 'When Beetleback Chief enters the battlefield, create two 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.', 'When Black Cat dies, target opponent discards a card at random.', 'When Bloodrage Brawler enters the battlefield, discard a card.', "When Brightmare enters the battlefield, tap up to one target creature. You gain life equal to that creature's power.", 'When Brindle Shoat dies, create a 3/3 green Boar creature token.', 'When Bulwark Giant enters the battlefield, you gain 5 life.', 'When Burglar Rat enters the battlefield, each opponent discards a card.', 'When Cauldron Familiar enters the battlefield, each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.\\nSacrifice a Food: Return Cauldron Familiar from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'When Corsair Captain enters the battlefield, create a Treasure token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")\\nOther Pirates you control get +1/+1.', "When Departed Deckhand becomes the target of a spell, sacrifice it.\\nDeparted Deckhand can't be blocked except by Spirits.\\n{3}{U}: Another target creature you control can't be blocked this turn except by Spirits.", "When Dinrova Horror enters the battlefield, return target permanent to its owner's hand, then that player discards a card.", 'When Drainpipe Vermin dies, you may pay {B}. If you do, target player discards a card.', 'When Dutiful Attendant dies, return another target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', "When Dwynen's Elite enters the battlefield, if you control another Elf, create a 1/1 green Elf Warrior creature token.", 'When Entomber Exarch enters the battlefield, choose one —\\n• Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.\\n• Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a noncreature card from it. That player discards that card.', "When Exclusion Mage enters the battlefield, return target creature an opponent controls to its owner's hand.", 'When Feral Prowler dies, draw a card.', 'When Festering Newt dies, target creature an opponent controls gets -1/-1 until end of turn. That creature gets -4/-4 instead if you control a creature named Bogbrew Witch.', 'When Flametongue Kavu enters the battlefield, it deals 4 damage to target creature.', 'When Forge Devil enters the battlefield, it deals 1 damage to target creature and 1 damage to you.', 'When Ghoulraiser enters the battlefield, return a Zombie card at random from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Goblin Commando enters the battlefield, it deals 2 damage to target creature.', 'When Goblin Instigator enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 red Goblin creature token.', "When Goblin Shortcutter enters the battlefield, target creature can't block this turn.", 'When Inspiring Captain enters the battlefield, creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'When Ironshell Beetle enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', 'When Lawless Broker dies, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control.', "When Lena, Selfless Champion enters the battlefield, create a 1/1 white Soldier creature token for each nontoken creature you control.\\nSacrifice Lena: Creatures you control with power less than Lena's power gain indestructible until end of turn.", 'When Living Lightning dies, return target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Mana Geode enters the battlefield, scry 1.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', "When Mausoleum Turnkey enters the battlefield, return target creature card of an opponent's choice from your graveyard to your hand.", 'When Meteor Golem enters the battlefield, destroy target nonland permanent an opponent controls.', 'When Miasmic Mummy enters the battlefield, each player discards a card.', 'When Muxus, Goblin Grandee enters the battlefield, reveal the top six cards of your library. Put all Goblin creature cards with mana value 5 or less from among them onto the battlefield and the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.\\nWhenever Muxus attacks, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn for each other Goblin you control.', 'When Myr Sire dies, create a 1/1 colorless Phyrexian Myr artifact creature token.', 'When Octoprophet enters the battlefield, scry 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them on the bottom of your library and the rest on top in any order.)', 'When Penumbra Bobcat dies, create a 2/1 black Cat creature token.', 'When Perilous Myr dies, it deals 2 damage to any target.', 'When Phyrexian Gargantua enters the battlefield, you draw two cards and you lose 2 life.', 'When Phyrexian Rager enters the battlefield, you draw a card and you lose 1 life.', "When Pirate's Cutlass enters the battlefield, attach it to target Pirate you control.\\nEquipped creature gets +2/+1.\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)", 'When Prophetic Prism enters the battlefield, draw a card.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.', 'When Prosperous Pirates enters the battlefield, create two Treasure tokens. (They\'re artifacts with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")', 'When Ravenous Chupacabra enters the battlefield, destroy target creature an opponent controls.', 'When Rishkar, Peema Renegade enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each of up to two target creatures.\\nEach creature you control with a counter on it has "{T}: Add {G}."', 'When Runed Servitor dies, each player draws a card.', "When Sage's Row Savant enters the battlefield, scry 2.", 'When Sailor of Means enters the battlefield, create a Treasure token. (It\'s an artifact with "{T}, Sacrifice this artifact: Add one mana of any color.")', 'When Sea Gate Oracle enters the battlefield, look at the top two cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the other on the bottom of your library.', "When Seismic Elemental enters the battlefield, creatures without flying can't block this turn.", 'When Shambling Goblin dies, target creature an opponent controls gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', 'When Silhana Wayfinder enters the battlefield, look at the top four cards of your library. You may reveal a creature or land card from among them and put it on top of your library. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order.', 'When Skittering Surveyor enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', "When Somberwald Stag enters the battlefield, you may have it fight target creature you don't control.", 'When Supply Runners enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on each other creature you control.', 'When Sylvan Brushstrider enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life.', 'When Sylvan Ranger enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Tempting Witch enters the battlefield, create a Food token. (It\'s an artifact with "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice this artifact: You gain 3 life.")\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice a Food: Target player loses 3 life.', 'When Thragtusk enters the battlefield, you gain 5 life.\\nWhen Thragtusk leaves the battlefield, create a 3/3 green Beast creature token.', "When Tibalt's Rager dies, it deals 1 damage to any target.\\n{1}{R}: Tibalt's Rager gets +2/+0 until end of turn.", 'When Tithebearer Giant enters the battlefield, you draw a card and you lose 1 life.', 'When Trusty Retriever enters the battlefield, choose one —\\n• Put a +1/+1 counter on Trusty Retriever.\\n• Return target artifact or enchantment card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Volley Veteran enters the battlefield, it deals damage to target creature an opponent controls equal to the number of Goblins you control.', 'When Wailing Ghoul enters the battlefield, mill two cards.', 'When Warfire Javelineer enters the battlefield, it deals X damage to target creature an opponent controls, where X is the number of instant and sorcery cards in your graveyard.', 'When you next cast an instant or sorcery spell this turn, copy that spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.', 'Whenever Ashmouth Hound blocks or becomes blocked by a creature, Ashmouth Hound deals 1 damage to that creature.', 'Whenever Blood Artist or another creature dies, target player loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever Borderland Marauder attacks, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', "Whenever Etali, Primal Storm attacks, exile the top card of each player's library, then you may cast any number of spells from among those cards without paying their mana costs.", "Whenever Initiate's Companion deals combat damage to a player, untap target creature or land.", 'Whenever Inspiring Unicorn attacks, creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Ornery Goblin blocks or becomes blocked by a creature, Ornery Goblin deals 1 damage to that creature.', 'Whenever Raging Regisaur attacks, it deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Whenever Selhoff Occultist or another creature dies, target player mills a card.', 'Whenever Sethron, Hurloon General or another nontoken Minotaur enters the battlefield under your control, create a 2/3 red Minotaur creature token.\\n{2}{B/R}: Minotaurs you control get +1/+0 and gain menace and haste until end of turn. ({B/R} can be paid with either {B} or {R}.)', 'Whenever Slate Street Ruffian becomes blocked, defending player discards a card.', 'Whenever Stone Haven Pilgrim attacks, if you control an artifact or enchantment, Stone Haven Pilgrim gets +1/+1 and gains lifelink until end of turn.', 'Whenever Towering-Wave Mystic deals damage, target player mills that many cards.', 'Whenever a creature dies, Gristle Grinner gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Whenever a creature dies, put a charge counter on Black Market.\\nAt the beginning of your precombat main phase, add {B} for each charge counter on Black Market.', 'Whenever a creature enters the battlefield under your control, put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control.', 'Whenever a creature you control deals combat damage to an opponent, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever an enchantment enters the battlefield under your control, create a 2/2 white Cat creature token. If that enchantment is an Aura, you may attach it to the token.', "Whenever an opponent casts a spell, reveal the top card of your library. If it's a creature card, put it onto the battlefield. Otherwise, you may put that card on the bottom of your library.", 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell, you may draw a card unless that player pays {1}.', 'Whenever an opponent draws their first card each turn, if it\'s not their turn, you create a 1/1 red Devil creature token with "When this creature dies, it deals 1 damage to any target."\\nWhenever one or more Devils you control attack one or more players, you and those players each draw a card, then discard a card at random.', 'Whenever an opponent loses life, you gain that much life.', "Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, its controller may draw a card if its power is greater than each other creature's power.\\n{G}, {T}: Add X mana in any combination of colors, where X is the greatest power among creatures you control.", "Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, you may put X +1/+1 counters on Hamletback Goliath, where X is that creature's power.", 'Whenever another creature with power 2 or less enters the battlefield under your control, you may pay {1}. If you do, draw a card.', 'Whenever another nontoken creature dies, you may create a 1/1 black Rat creature token.\\nRats you control have deathtouch.', 'Whenever equipped creature deals combat damage to a player, you may draw a card.\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Whenever one or more creatures attack, you may have target attacking creature gain double strike until end of turn.', "Whenever one or more creatures you control fight or become blocked, draw a card.\\nAt the beginning of combat on your turn, you may pay {2}{R/G}. If you do, double target creature's power until end of turn. That creature must be blocked this combat if able. ({R/G} can be paid with either {R} or {G}.)", 'Whenever one or more non-Human creatures you control deal combat damage to a player, draw a card.', "Whenever you cast a creature spell with power 4, 5, or 6, Sarkhan's Unsealing deals 4 damage to any target.\\nWhenever you cast a creature spell with power 7 or greater, Sarkhan's Unsealing deals 4 damage to each opponent and each creature and planeswalker they control.", 'Whenever you cast a creature spell, create a 3/3 green Beast creature token.\\nWhenever you cast a noncreature spell, put three +1/+1 counters on target creature you control.\\nLandfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 3 life.', 'Whenever you cast a creature spell, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, Cathar\'s Companion gains indestructible until end of turn. (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy it.)', 'Whenever you cast an artifact spell, draw a card.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Kiln Fiend gets +3/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create a 1/1 red Elemental creature token.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, create a 2/2 blue Drake creature token with flying.', 'Whenever you gain life, Kalastria Nightwatch gains flying until end of turn.', 'Whenever you gain life, put a +1/+1 counter on Bloodbond Vampire.', 'Whenever you gain life, you may pay {1}{W}. If you do, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature for each 1 life you gained.', "Wight of Precinct Six gets +1/+1 for each creature card in your opponents' graveyards.", 'You draw two cards, lose 2 life, then mill two cards.', 'You may play an additional land on each of your turns.\\nPlay with the top card of your library revealed.\\nYou may play lands from the top of your library.', 'You may play an additional land this turn.\\nDraw a card.', '{1}, Sacrifice Scroll of Avacyn: Draw a card. If you control an Angel, you gain 5 life.', '{1}, Sacrifice a Scarecrow: Draw a card.\\n{4}, {T}: Return target artifact creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', '{1}, Sacrifice a creature: Put a +1/+1 counter on Phyrexian Broodlings.', '{1}, Sacrifice an artifact or creature: Makeshift Munitions deals 1 damage to any target.', '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Chromatic Sphere: Add one mana of any color. Draw a card.', '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: You gain 4 life.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature named Festering Newt: Each opponent loses 4 life. You gain life equal to the life lost this way.', '{1}{B}, Pay 2 life: Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{1}{B}, Sacrifice another creature: Put a +1/+1 counter on Blood Host and you gain 2 life.', '{1}{R}{R}: Pyroclastic Elemental deals 1 damage to target player.', '{1}{U}, {T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{1}{W}: Target creature you control gains lifelink until end of turn. (Damage dealt by the creature also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', '{2}, {T}: Each opponent loses 1 life and you gain 1 life.', '{2}, {T}: Search your library for a card named Festering Newt or Bubbling Cauldron, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{2}{B}, Sacrifice Corpse Hauler: Return another target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{2}{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a card from it. That player discards that card. Activate only as a sorcery.', '{2}{B}: Return Sanitarium Skeleton from your graveyard to your hand.', "{2}{G}: Target creature you control can't be blocked by creatures with power 2 or less this turn.", '{3}, {T}: Draw a card.', "{3}: Exile another target creature you control, then return it to the battlefield under its owner's control.\\nWhenever another creature enters the battlefield under your control, you may pay {G/W}. If you do, put a +1/+1 counter on it. If it's a Unicorn, put two +1/+1 counters on it instead. ({G/W} can be paid with either {G} or {W}.)", '{3}: Jousting Dummy gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "{3}{B}, Exile Ghoulcaller's Accomplice from your graveyard: Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token. Activate only as a sorcery.", '{3}{U}{U}: Draw two cards.', '{5}, {T}, Sacrifice Lightning-Core Excavator: It deals 3 damage to any target.', '{8}: Target creature gets +5/+5 and gains trample until end of turn.', '{B}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', "{B}, {T}, Sacrifice another creature: Create X 2/2 black Zombie creature tokens, where X is the sacrificed creature's power.", '{G}, Sacrifice Dawntreader Elk: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{R}, Sacrifice Torch Fiend: Destroy target artifact.', '{R}, Sacrifice a creature: Barrage of Expendables deals 1 damage to any target.', '{R}, {T}, Exile two cards from your graveyard: Grim Lavamancer deals 2 damage to any target.', '{R}: Molten Ravager gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{T}, Sacrifice Terramorphic Expanse: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color.\\n{T}: Target creature becomes the color or colors of your choice until end of turn.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}{U}, {T}: Return target Wizard you control to its owner's hand.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Buried Ruin: Return target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{7}, {T}, Sacrifice Unstable Obelisk: Destroy target permanent.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Add {B}{B}.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Put a charge counter on Mirrodin's Core.\\n{T}, Remove a charge counter from Mirrodin's Core: Add one mana of any color.", '{T}: Add {C}{C}.\\n{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Hedron Archive: Draw two cards.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}{C}.\\n{3}, {T}, Sacrifice Dreamstone Hedron: Draw three cards.', '{T}: Add {G}.', "{T}: Bloodshot Trainee deals 4 damage to target creature. Activate only if Bloodshot Trainee's power is 4 or greater.", '{T}: Create X 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens, where X is the number of Goblins you control.', "{T}: Draw a card and reveal it. If it isn't a land card, discard it.", '{T}: Scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)', '{T}: Target player draws a card, then discards a card.', "{U}, Sacrifice Aether Spellbomb: Return target creature to its owner's hand.\\n{1}, Sacrifice Aether Spellbomb: Draw a card.", '{U}, {T}: Target player mills two cards.', '{X}{R}, {T}, Sacrifice Cinder Elemental: It deals X damage to any target.']
flavor: ['". . . and furthermore . . ."', '"Accursed scarecrow! Sending folk in every direction is the same as sending them nowhere at all."\\n—Corliss the Wanderer', '"Aether is the soul of Kaladesh, and all souls should be free."', '"All we know about the Krosan Forest we have learned from those few who made it out alive."\\n—Elvish refugee', '"Alone, it\'s a fortification. At the head of its troops, it\'s a battering ram."\\n—Skerk Hobnett, wilderness guide', '"Always carry two spears."\\n—Mokgar, Kalonian hunter', '"Any ship that sails on these mean seas for long is bound to pick up a ghost or two."\\n—Admiral Beckett Brass', '"As expected, this sphere\'s design reflects the colors of the four moons . . . plus another?"\\n—Pontifex, elder researcher', '"As you inject the *viscus vitae* into the brain stem, don\'t let the spastic moaning bother you. It will soon become music to your ears."\\n—Stitcher Geralf', '"Bant\'s most gallant knights wear my sigil, and for that I am humbled."', '"Behind every devil\'s mayhem lurks a demon\'s scheme."\\n—Rem Karolus, Blade of the Inquisitors', '"Can\'t a fella get a moment\'s peace around here?"', '"Charge bravely. Fight selflessly. Act honorably. Iroas will watch over you."\\n—Verenis, priest of Iroas', '"Come. Bring your brothers. Tonight, you feast on living flesh."\\n—Jadar, ghoulcaller of Nephalia', '"Death—an outmoded concept. We sleep, and we change."\\n—Sitrik, birth priest', '"Do not mistake a quiet rampart for one that is unguarded. Some things stir only when they need to."\\n—Bonovar, siege commander', '"Do not mistake your lofty vantage point for safety."\\n—Shaper Tuvasa', '"Don\'t let it fool you. Many of us got our first scars from Syr Nobody."\\n—Syr Layne, knight of Embereth', '"Don\'t worry, sweet brother. Help is on the way."\\n—Ghoulcaller Gisa', '"Even rats hoard their treasures. Are your precious things so different?"\\n—Izoni', '"Even storm clouds bow to worship Avacyn."\\n—Elder Rimheit', '"Every choice alters the path of fate."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"Fill the sky with stuff!"', '"Finally, a weapon the Boros can\'t confiscate!"\\n—Juri, proprietor of the Juri Revue', '"Find out whose that is. I like its energy."\\n—Judith', '"Fire will cure a multitude of ills."', '"Fools dig for water, corpses, or gold. The earth\'s real treasure is far deeper."', '"For dim-witted, thick-skulled genetic mutants, they have pretty good aim."\\n—Sisay, captain of the *Weatherlight*', '"For every living person there are generations of dead. Which realm would you rather rule?"\\n—Liliana Vess', '"Geralf, must you always whine? I agreed to nothing. I\'ll raise ghouls anytime I wish."', '"Grease up a firecannon good and proper with dinosaur-liver oil, and it\'ll shoot just about anything."', '"Great art can never be created without great suffering."', '"He displays a perverse charisma fueled by avarice. Highly dangerous. Recommend civil sanctions."\\n—Agmand Sarv, Azorius hussar', '"He expects a reward, but the only piece of silver he\'ll get from me is my blade in his gut."\\n—Shelac, necromancer', '"He is judge, jury, and executioner because he killed them all."\\n—Bishop Cawle of Elgaud', '"Here lies Gond, hero of Safehold Taldwen. May he ever guide our quest."', '"His tenement is filled with the most vile, disgusting vermin. It\'s infested with rats, too."\\n—Branko One-Ear', '"Horse? Who needs a horse?"', '"How can we outrun the sky?"\\n—Hadran, sunseeder of Naya', '"I believe many worlds will bow to Phyrexia. Mirrodin is merely the first."\\n—Sheoldred, Whispering One', '"I can see why this appeals to Thassa."\\n—Kiora', '"I can think of no greater punishment than answering your question in full."\\n—Lazav', '"I do not lead. They do not follow. We walk together."', '"I don\'t care if it\'s an all-powerful relic or a street vendor\'s lucky charm. If it brings you courage, wear it."\\n—Saheeli Rai', '"I don\'t like to think of myself as a pirate. I\'m more like a stimulator of the local economy."', '"I fight for Keranos and for mortals. I see no contradiction."', '"I often think on how excited they must feel to be chosen as my prey."', '"I see a spark of pure rage. Soon that spark will spread from the depths of Kragma. Soon its fire will engulf the polis."\\n—Hira, street oracle', '"I see countless worlds. What makes them think I can\'t find them in just one?"\\n—Ral Zarek', '"I was wrong. Zendikar isn\'t after me. It isn\'t after any of us. It\'s not evil or vengeful. It\'s magnificent . . . but it\'s in pain."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"I will not live as a slave. If you would be free, then fight alongside me."', '"I\'d like to say that it\'s our pet, but the reverse may be closer to the truth."\\n—Ixor, initiate of Rhet crop', '"I\'m not running away! I\'m figuring out the best routes."', '"I\'ve always said full war chests win wars, but I didn\'t mean by bashing enemy skulls with them."\\n—Teysa', '"If you can\'t control your mount, I will control it for you."\\n—Mirela, Azorius hussar', '"If you live on a giant\'s back, there\'s only one individual you\'ll ever need to fear."\\n—Gaddock Teeg', '"If you threaten its territory, it produces spores. Actually, no matter what you do, it produces spores."\\n—Hadi Kasten, Calla Dale naturalist', '"In these halls there is no pass or fail. Your true test comes with the first full moon."', '"Is it the water? The stars? Whatever it is, something incredible is happening here."\\n—Eris, zoologist, journal entry', '"It appears that nature has risen against us."\\n—Captain Brinely Rage', '"It has been my experience that disasters like to strike in pairs."', '"It wandered slowly across the landscape, calling out in its lonely voice, but no other castles answered its cries."\\n—*Beyond the Great Henge*', '"It was right here a second ago . . ."', '"It\'s cold in the grave, and the dead crave your warmth. Who are you to deny them?"\\n—Strava, Dimir mage', '"It\'s so cute when it\'s sleeping, isn\'t it? Actually, it\'s still as abhorrent as ever, but at least it\'s not trying to kill us."\\n—Noyan Dar, Tazeem lullmage', '"It\'s time for the \'Smash, Smash\' song!"', '"Just as a broken relic can be mended, a shattered history can be made whole."', '"Just think how strong I\'ll be if my arms don\'t tear off!"', '"Kalitas may have returned to mindless servitude beneath the Eldrazi, but we say never again."\\n—Drana, Kalastria bloodchief', '"Knock, knock."', '"Let the vampires join us. In this war, we no longer have the luxury of choosing our comrades."\\n—General Tazri, allied commander', '"Life as we know it dangles on the brink of extinction. We must show the strength they would steal from us."\\n—*The Invokers\' Tales*', '"Lightning in a bottle? That\'s not where I need it."', '"Llanowar\'s boughs are ever ready\\nTo unleash an autumn of steel leaves."\\n—"Song of Freyalise"', '"Look at her, once filled with innocence. Death has a way of wringing away such . . . deficiencies."\\n—Savra', '"Lungs full of sea air and a hold full of loot. Ah, what a life!"', '"Madness can\'t touch a mind ignited by genius."', '"May all the cairns of Jund be toppled."\\n—Meren of Clan Nel Toth', '"Merciless to the point of psychosis. Let\'s give him a job."\\n—Zelinas, Orzhov recruiter', '"Most faeries are harmless pranksters. Every now and again, though, you get one that crosses over from mischievous to malicious."\\n—Gaddock Teeg', '"Murder clad in crimson beauty,\\nAn end to life and love and duty."\\n—Barrow witch incantation', '"My \'condition\' is a trial. The weak are consumed by it. The strong transcend it."\\n—Sorin Markov', '"My faith is stronger than fang, claw, or mindless hunger."', '"My heart and Zendikar\'s beat as one. Together we will endure."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"My secret ingredient? Well, I can\'t tell you that. But here\'s a hint. It\'s not love."', '"My visions don\'t show me home. They show me where home is yet to be found."', '"Nice army you had there."', '"Nobody ever listens to my complaints! Not even when I use the listening stick."', '"Not all paths are found on the forest floor."', '"Now is the hour. Ours is the duty. For victory and family—charge!"', '"Oh, it\'s easy enough to kill, but I\'m not going anywhere near it."\\n—Norin the Wary', '"Oh, you must be mistaken. Hawks are solitary hunters, you see."\\n—Bunder Diedreck, ornithologist', '"Once in the box, we\'re all the same."', '"Only the foolhardy would venture into the Akoum Mountains without a lullmage to tame the raging rocks and living fires."\\n—Sachir, Akoum Expeditionary House', '"Only the lion knows more stories than I do."\\n—Chulane, Teller of Tales', '"Our enemy is nothing less than the end of all life. We shall not want for allies."\\n—*The War Diaries*', '"Peril is in the eye of the beholder. At least, if your aim is good."\\n—Jaya Ballard', '"Please don\'t feed the beetles."\\n—Promenade warning sign', '"Release that which was never caged."\\n—Spellbomb inscription', '"Soulless demon, you are bound to me. Now we will both dwell in oblivion."', '"Stay close! It\'s just a little farther."', '"Surely it won\'t notice if I take—"\\n—Theria the Sly, last words', '"Surely you know the joy of the hunt, my furry friend. My kind of hunt just takes a different form than yours."', '"Terrifying, but thankfully temporary."\\n—Teferi', '"That\'s the third time this month it\'s exploded on site. Maybe we should switch to something a little less defective."\\n—Kerrin, archaeologist', '"The Brazen Coalition is a firecannon pointed at our enemies. Goblins like him are the spark to its powder."\\n—Admiral Beckett Brass', '"The Knowledge Pool knows. Memnarch understands."\\n—Janus, speaker of the synod', '"The Kolaghan send them at us. We kill and raise them. They fight the next wave the Kolaghan send. It\'s a neat little cycle."\\n—Asmala, Silumgar sorcerer', '"The coronation of King Numsgil, no . . . adventures of Tuktuk, no . . . the saga of Morpo the Bard, no! Where\'s *my* story?"', '"The endurance of the ancient turtles in a land so harsh makes a strong case for patience, tranquility, and composure."\\n—Gavi, nest warden', '"The explorer who found it got a bad deal when he sold it. He merely got rich."', '"The first rule of politics can be learned from a lowly hornbeetle: it is wise to cultivate powerful friends."\\n—Pythamon, sage of Meletis', '"The gods don\'t speak to mortals with gentle entreaties. They speak with thunder and fury."', '"The greatest gift Dromoka gives is the ability to fly without wings."\\n—Urdnan, Dromoka warrior', '"The hardest thing is finding the right ingredients."', '"The land has its own intentions, beyond the understanding of those who live on it."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"The mist whispers to those who know it to be more than a mundane fog."', '"The most insidious thing in the world is nonsense that sounds just plausible enough to listen to."\\n—Lazav', '"The old gods awoke and sent fingers of fire to see what was left of the old ways under the endless city."\\n—Daiva, Gruul storyteller', '"The people of Akros must learn from our leonin adversaries. If we match their staunch ferocity with our superior faith, we cannot fail."\\n—Cymede, queen of Akros', '"The predator knows the true way of the world. Life is conflict. Only the strong survive."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"The seas are vast, but the skies are even more so. Why be content with one kingdom when I can rule them both?"', '"The second mage learned to dissipate blasts of lightning. Threat and response: thus did the study of magic progress."\\n—Naban, dean of iteration', '"The second stage of the illness: high fever and severe infectiousness."\\n—Phyrexian progress notes', '"The secret entrance should be near."', '"The world is a puzzle, and the mind is its key."', '"Their only dreams are of full stomachs."\\n—Kleon the Iron-Booted', '"There are only fifty words in the cyclops language, and ten of them mean \'kill.\'"\\n—Ertai', '"There it was, clawing the ice as it chittered and clicked its teeth. We fled in horror before it unearthed its grisly meal."\\n—Aevar Borg, northern guide, journal entry', '"There\'s a smoothness to my magic here that I don\'t find on any other plane."', '"They are called Eternals. They will never stop."\\n—Jace Beleren', '"They are deadly, and they are loyal. We can spare them a little blood."\\n—Harak, Malakir bloodwitch', '"This is just my warm-up."', '"Those dragons grow fast. For a while they feed on squirrels and goblins and then suddenly you\'re missing a mammoth."\\n—Hurdek, Mazar mammoth trainer', '"Those who do evil and those who do nothing are equally worthy of contempt."', '"Those wings are no advantage. I will pin them to the ceiling of the Hekma."', '"Time to show the foe our true mettle."', '"To truly know something, you must become it. The trick is to not lose yourself in the process."', '"Trying to stop it would be foolish. If you feel it coming—run!"\\n—Sergeant Ryda', '"United, our roar will level mountains."', '"Unwavering and loyal, they represent stability in uncertain times."\\n—Rem Karolus, Slayer of Angels', '"We are armed with light and steel. Who can stand against us?"', '"We can take \'em. You go first!"', '"We hold sacred the powers of light and life. Truth and honor are our greatest weapons."\\n—Alabaster creed', '"We must all make sacrifices for the good of Innistrad."\\n—Sorin Markov', '"We speak the dragons\' language of flame and rage. They speak our language of fury and honor. Together we shall weave a tale of destruction without equal."', '"Welcome to the Dimir Public Offices. Not responsible for death or loss of property. Basement off-limits."\\n—Sign outside Dinrova Building', '"Welcome to the Legion. You saved a district—now let\'s go save the world."', '"Well, this can\'t be a good sign."\\n—Old Rutstein', '"Where did *she* come from? More importantly, are there more like her?"\\n—Gideon Jura', '"Where metal is tainted and wood is scarce, we are best armed by faith."\\n—Tavalus, acolyte of Korlis', '"Where will you run when I punish you with the very ground you flee on?"\\n—Nicol Bolas', '"Which do you deserve, the heft of a femur or the graceful sharpness of a forearm? Decisions, decisions . . ."\\n—Gisa the Mad', '"Whoever thought of making mobile volcanoes was a genius."\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"Why perch in the crow\'s nest when I can fly like the crows?"', '"Within each of you is the strength of a landslide."\\n—Kumano, to his pupils', '"Yawgmoth is dead, and his citadels lie empty. But there will always be some who seek power at any price."\\n—Karn', '"You bound me with a contract only your death could end—and you thought me the fool?"\\n—Liliana Vess', '"You have done your best. I give you leave to rest."', '"You have led us to triumph over the forces of Mogis!" said Brygus the Brave, clapping the Champion on the back. The Champion wiped the sweat and blood from her brow. "I count eight graves," she said. "Too many to call this a victory."\\n—*The Theriad*', '"You have to admit, Gideon—he has great form."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"You won\'t need the sword drills, your shields, or my blessing. You\'ll fight for Sunhome with the truth in your heart."\\n—Aurelia', '"You\'d better be worth it."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"You\'re in luck. I brought enough to share."\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"You\'ve begun to understand the hedrons\' true purpose," said Ugin. "The Eldrazi can be imprisoned."\\n"And how did that work out last time?" asked Jace.', '"Your death will take a mere moment, but it will feel like an eternity."\\n—Vilis, Broker of Blood', '"Your mind is too filled with foolish concerns to hear the subtle whispers that the breeze brings."', 'A bit of pain never hurts.', 'A few aetherborn have discovered a way to sustain their own existences at the cost of an insatiable hunger for the life essence of other beings.', 'A living pulse is an irresistible temptation.', 'A minotaur does not distinguish between human, satyr, and triton. They are all meat.', 'A momentary lapse is all it needs to break free.', 'A ray of hope in the darkest night.', 'A sharp axe solves most problems.', 'A spirit is both fettered and free—bound in some ways to its previous existence, yet able to transcend much of the corporeal.', 'After Talrand conquered the depths of Shandalar, his ambitions drove him skyward, joined by servants whose drive and curiosity equaled his own.', 'All are prey to the eyes of the wild.', 'All the books were dusty with disuse, save the one titled *Camouflage and Its Practical Applications*.', 'All the wonders of the natural world in one breathtaking microcosm.', "Amonkhet's dual suns don't allow for the darkness of night, so bats are most active under the gloom of the frequent sandstorms.", 'An Izzet experiment begins with a "what if," gets approved with a "why not," and concludes with a "eureka!"', "An explorer's reward is a view of tomorrow's possibilities.", "As eons passed, the rock wore away, revealing the rich colors at the mountain's heart.", 'As the shards merged into the Maelstrom, their mana energies fused into new monstrosities.', 'Atarka goblins meet their demise as readily as their Temur counterparts did, but usually under big, winged shadows.', 'Atarka serving-goblins coat themselves with grease imbued with noxious herbs, hoping to discourage their ravenous masters from adding them to the meal.', "Avacyn's holy warriors kept hope alive in her darkest hours. Now they will carry that hope across Innistrad.", "Baby dragons can't figure out humans—if they didn't want to be killed, why were they made of meat and treasure?", 'Beauty appears in strange places for those with eyes to see it.', 'Big distractions mean tiny nuisances can slip by unnoticed.', 'Born of volcanic forces, it thrives on the absolute panic it inspires.', 'Call one, call them all.', 'Caught between life and death, between land and sea, between thought and oblivion.', 'Death is no excuse to stop working.', 'Despite the reemergence of werewolves and the proliferation of Eldrazi, elk numbers in the Somberwald have remained steady.', 'Devils redecorate every room with fire.', 'Devils sow chaos and reap panic.', 'Dragonslayers learned to keep silent about their deeds after seeing the terrible vengeance wrought by Kolaghan and her brood.', "Drakes become especially voracious as they prepare for their autumn migration, hunting the city's thoroughfares from dawn to dusk.", 'Each flower identical, every leaf and petal disturbingly exact.', 'Each spell is an intricate tapestry, and Kira is the great unraveler.', 'Eidren, perfect of Lys Alana, ordered hundreds of trees uprooted and rearranged into a pattern he deemed beautiful. Thus the Gilt-Leaf Wood was born.', 'Empires rise and fall, but evil is eternal.', 'Even as humans regained the upper hand, some still willingly traded their lives for a chance at immortality.', 'Even the lost and undead need a protector.', "Every day the cat returns to kill the same mouse, which sinks again into the cauldron's brew.", 'Every tear shed is a drop of immortality.', 'Everyone who could still lift a weapon had a part in retaking Sea Gate.', 'Fairgoers were delighted to find that even outside the fairgrounds, Ghirapur was a city of wonders.', 'Far from human eyes, birds flit between vivid blossoms in a hidden paradise.', 'First the insult, then the encore.', 'For Mittens, it was just another day at the beach.', 'For each creature that arrives in its audience, the sage imparts another piece of ancient wisdom for all to hear.', 'For the Phyrexians, death is not an end, nor a one-time occurrence.', 'Friends teach what you want to know. Enemies teach what you *need* to know.', 'Funerary masks help the newly dead resist the erosion of memory and identity in the Underworld.', "Goblin generals don't distinguish between troops and ammunition.", 'Good dogs stay by your side until the end. Great dogs leave to bring back aid.', "He has the biggest bashing stick, so it's a safe bet he's the leader.", 'He knows the name of every elf born in the last four centuries. More importantly, they all know his.', 'Her horn is heard across Innistrad, lifting the hearts of the righteous.', 'Her poppets bring joy to the truly depraved.', 'His mind was lost long before his flesh.', 'History has buried its treasures deep.', 'Hunters lure the stripling boar into the open, hoping to trap greater prey.', 'If only every message were as perfect as its bearer.', 'Immolation is the sincerest form of flattery.', 'Imprisonment teaches revenge. Hobbling teaches resignation.', 'In dark times, Truth bears a blade.', 'In every swirl of the tide, it sees the awakening of things yet to come.', 'In his hands, the wind can become a weapon or a means of escape.', 'In the Gudul delta, bloodfly bites are indistinguishable from spear wounds.', 'In the dim light beneath the vast trees of Deepglade, baloths prowl in search of prey. Their guttural calls are more felt than heard, but their attack scream carries for miles.', "In the hold of the *Heart of Kiran*, Chandra answered Dovin Baan's sabotage with an explosive retort.", 'In the quiet before a battle, Boros soldiers whisper prayers that steady their nerves and focus their minds.', 'In times of infestation and war, Zendikar favors the blades that strike in unison.', 'Inner strength is never seen until it makes all the difference.', "It carries the hopes of Zendikar's embattled wilds on its mighty boughs.", 'It glides on silent wings across the midnight sky, and a dread host rises to follow.', 'It is much easier to create fire than to contain it.', 'It manifests at wizard academies to siphon inspiration from young prodigies.', 'It returns eager to share the feast of blood and gore with its ghoulish master.', 'It shreds its prey as each head fights for the choicest bits.', 'It slithers through the senses, constricting consciousness and poisoning perceptions.', 'It traps an explosion within its stony skin.', "It wasn't long until the elves had developed a use for every part of the Eldrazi.", 'It would be ill-mannered to decline his invitation. It would be ill-advised to accept it.', "It's there when a seed sprouts, when gourds ripen on the vines, and when the reapers cut the grains under the Harvest Moon.", "Its back bubbles like a witch's cauldron, and it smells just as vile.", "Its breath doesn't assault the senses. It pollutes the mind.", 'Its breath is a gale. Its roar is a volcano. Its anger tears soul from flesh.', 'Its collapse is like the lashing out of a long-dead civilization that resents being forgotten.', 'Its fiery paws make it easy to track, which is very useful when you want to go in exactly the opposite direction.', 'Its footsteps of today are the lakes of tomorrow.', 'Its last life is spent tormenting your dreams.', 'Kaladesh\'s illicit marketplaces are known as "night markets," but if you know who to ask, you can find what you\'re looking for at any time of the day.', 'Knowledge itself is neither good nor evil. Just as the wrong book in the wrong hands could doom all existence, the same book in the right hands could save it.', "Kruphix hid the most dire prophecies about humankind where humans would never find them and tritons wouldn't care to read them.", 'Life is such a fragile thing.', "Life's too short to not do the things you love.", 'Like a cross between a spider and a spyglass, but friendlier.', 'Like all jungle plants, the vines must fight and claw for sunlight. Once their place is secured, they grow strong, sharp, and impenetrable.', 'Like blinking or breathing, responding to an alarm is an involuntary reflex.', "Liliana is never one to follow someone else's lead.", 'Magic written across the sky falls like rain on thirsty ground, bringing forth wisdom in its season.', 'Magistrate Ludy agreed to designate land for the brushstriders only after several broken windows and dozens of missing blini-cakes.', 'Many a besieged city has surrendered upon hearing the distinctive rumble of the juggernaut.', 'Many elves incorporate the beauty of nature into their inventions. Very few capture its savagery.', 'Many hands for many evils.', 'May the worthy spend an eternity in Blessed Sleep. May the wicked find the peace of oblivion.', 'Minotaurs favor magic that manifests as weapons wrapped in flame.', 'Nature abhors a zombie.', "Naya's trees grow tall and sturdy. Their foliage intertwines to form dewcups, rainwater pools where the elves gather to celebrate life.", 'Never flinch. Never falter. Never fear.', 'No guilds—that is her rule. The House vampires unnerve her. The Combine would dissect her, the Legion burn her, the Conclave "cure" her. The shadows are all the family she needs.', 'Not all heroes die in armor.', 'Not all storms come from the sky.', 'Not content to nudge vases and chill drawing rooms, some geists muster spectral armies to claw at the hearts of the living.', "Not even the tallest tree stands a chance against the underside of a dinosaur's foot.", "Nylea's sacred lynx guards those who honor the Nessian Wood and hunts those who don't.", 'On Evos Isle, the swift and formidable aven enforce the will of the ruling sphinxes.', 'Once a welcoming hub for explorers, Affa became a place of guarded tongues and quick defenses.', 'Once favored companions, many cats were left to fend for themselves.', 'One day, they may be paragons of deadly elegance. For the moment, they possess nothing but thirst.', 'Only the Eldrazi mind thinks in the warped paths required to open the hedrons and tap the power within.', 'Opening Orazca unleashed more horrors than just the Immortal Sun.', 'Other Phyrexians have nightmares about the gargantua.', 'Philosophers say those lost at sea ascended to a more perfect realm. Sailors say they drowned.', 'Predicting the future is a messy business.', 'Progress comes at a price.', 'Pure souls shine bright as daybreak.', "Ravnica's defenders watched in horror as Oketra's shot pierced the body of the pegasus. Gideon tumbled through the air, Blackblade in hand.", "Rhonas's monument is home to a wider variety of creatures than anywhere else in the city of Naktamun—a feature most initiates fail to appreciate.", 'Rhoxes who live long enough to retire from war lend support with their extensive knowledge of combat injuries.', 'Scholars had puzzled for centuries over the ruins at Tal Terig. Its secrets had always lived within one rune-carved head.', 'Scream: muffled. Pockets: emptied. Neck function: never the same again.', 'Seen through Rakdos eyes, a cruel betrayal is a hilarious stunt.', 'She arrived like a meteorite, and the enemy fell in a shock wave of holy vengeance.', 'She reaches beyond the physical realm, touching the ideals from which all creatures draw their power.', 'She yearned to walk on dry land so she might take her vengeance there.', 'Silent as winter snow, it seeks wild places unspoiled by the walking dead.', 'So-called "old wood" is rare in deforested Ravnica. Statues carved from it are said to house the last of the ancient nature spirits.', 'Some Akroans make the dangerous pilgrimage to the volcanic temples of Purphoros, where oracles known as flamespeakers glean omens from lava.', 'Spirits disturbed by ghoulcallers become geists driven by restless anger.', "Successful battles start with knowing who's worth fighting.", 'Summoners of efreeti remember only the power of command, never the sting of regret.', "Takedowns in Valor's Reach are never meant to be lethal, but that doesn't mean they won't be incredibly painful.", "Thassa's favor followed him to the Underworld. Even the waves of Nerono obeyed his will.", "The Boros built a prison in the sky where Azorius statutes couldn't restrict their sense of justice.", "The Mardu warrior was overjoyed when Tasigur set him free and granted him passage through the jungle. He failed to notice the Sultai leader's cruel smile.", 'The Roil takes many forms. It also takes many victims.', 'The aberrant magic of the Rimewind drew the unicorns back from the northern wastes to do battle once again.', 'The angel remembers her past lives like dreams. Her song held up meadows. Her blade drove back darkness. Her wings carried her across the ages.', "The baloth's instincts boiled, its muscles pulled taut, and its razor-spines bristled, as it turned to face—a runt meepling.", 'The best defense is a good offense.', 'The best engineers recognize when a problem has already been solved.', 'The best techniques outlive their creators.', 'The daredevil racers of the Derby Crows, long at odds with the Consulate, were quick to join the renegades in open revolt.', 'The defenders watched in terror as the flying V split apart into a bristling battle formation.', 'The delight of discovery drives the pursuit of knowledge.', 'The devil appreciated the irony of using doves for ammunition. The townsfolk, not so much.', "The dragon who eats the last head in the basket is entitled to the servant's.", 'The druids of Mazar treat each seedcone with respect for the warrior it will become.', 'The earth walks, strongest of all.', 'The first mistake the Grimnant knights made was bullying the owner of an Urborg corpse shop. Their second mistake was dying.', "The floating city of High and Dry hasn't yet sunk under the weight of gold, but it's not for want of trying.", 'The frillbacks of Orazca soak up the sun on their tall spinal fins. They look slow and sleepy—until they catch the scent of prey.', 'The hound sniffed the air and let slip a low growl. General Takeno looked down at the faithful Isamaru and calmed him with a touch. "Alert the guard. The kami are coming."', 'The idols were forged during the time of the Khanfall, when the dragons came to rule Tarkir and its people aligned themselves with the five dragonlords.', 'The impact sent the soldiers scattering—then something came out of the crater.', 'The mage awakened the statue in hopes of learning the lost lore of her clan, but the statue was interested only in war.', 'The mage looked within and realized there was still one piece of fuel to burn.', "The most frightening storms are those not woven by nature's hand.", 'The mournful lowing of brushstriders warns of changing weather and ill winds.', 'The mouth must be pried open before rigor mortis sets in. Otherwise the returning soul can find no ingress.', "The nomads' funeral pyres are more practical than ceremonial.", 'The people of Tarkir speak of an ancient legend, of the dragon-man called Sarkhan who was greatest of all khans.', 'The persistence to overcome obstacles is the most esteemed of kor virtues.', 'The person who finishes a journey is rarely the same as the one who starts it.', 'The power of the wild, concentrated in a single charge.', "The problem isn't the indrik's enthusiasm, it's Ravnica's lack of guardrails.", "The rising tide of Orazca's plunder lifted all ships.", 'The scent of cooked flesh lingers in the charred landscape of Tarkir.', "The sparkmage shrieked, calling on the rage of the storms of his youth. To his surprise, the sky responded with a fierce energy he'd never thought to see again.", 'The storm rages and the earth breaks.', 'The streets of Ravnica are full of former guild members now using their institutional skills for personal gain.', 'The trick to talking sense into Keldons is getting them to hold still.', "The unicorns of Sursi are a manifestation of Serra's joy and compassion. They frolic and dance like children, offering blessings to anyone they encounter.", 'The unlabeled vial was not vanilla extract after all.', "The view is truly spectacular—as long as you don't look at Rishada itself.", 'The wounded see the glow of its vials long before they see its wings diving out of the clouds.', 'Their denial reaches far into your future.', 'There are two lives: the life you live before you see a unicorn, and the life you live after.', 'There is no world where angels fear to tread.', 'They are the first to greet dissenters on their journey into exile.', 'They charge into battle and out for their morning walk with the same exuberance.', 'Thievery requires subtlety, from the beginning of the heist to the end.', "This cat has two lives and it's hunting for more.", 'Those who intrude upon the Dimir seldom remember that they have done so.', 'Those who seek to disturb the harmony of life will see their instruments taken from them.', "Those without breath can't complain.", 'Though she is rightly feared, there are relatively few tales of her deeds in battle, for few survive her raids.', 'To Hazoret, those who fight for her are her beloved children.', 'To Mirrodin, an explosive. To Phyrexia, a missionary.', 'Treefolk and elves share a common interest in the forests, but really the elves just feel at home with the view from above.', 'Two times the size, four times the smell.', 'Until Emeria is freed, he raises his sword in her name.', 'Upon such armor, even a mountain would break.', "Were she not a judge, she'd win the division herself.", 'When Selesnya missionaries moved into the Shanav Quarter, they faced scorn, ridicule, and ultimately martyrdom.', 'When he reaches for his key ring, you should be running for the exit.', 'When times are tough, the poor eat the rats. When times are tougher, the rats eat the poor.', 'Whether mechanical or biological, life finds a way to propagate itself.', 'Whether trained, ridden, or eaten, few goblin military innovations have rivaled the bug.', 'While other pirates prowl for treasure, Captain Parrish plunders secrets.', 'Wildflowers here bloom not with the season but with the ebb and flow of magic.', "Wipe away the slobber and it's as good as new, give or take a few bite marks.", "With a commando around, somebody's gonna get hurt.", 'With five lenses on its "head," it sees the world in a range of colors beyond ordinary perception.', 'With limited resources and near unlimited time, Kerrick used parts from one beast to build another.', 'With or without witnesses, the suns continued their prismatic dance.', 'Words to bless the eye that reads them, telling of a future beyond the reach of fear.', "You don't so much hire goblins as put ideas in their heads.", 'Zombies mourn for the living and celebrate those who will soon be given the gift of death.']
artist: ['Aaron Miller', 'Adam Paquette', 'Adi Granov', 'Alan Pollack', 'Alayna Danner', 'Alejandro Mirabal', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Alex Konstad', 'Anastasia Ovchinnikova', 'Andreas Rocha', 'Anna Steinbauer', 'Anthony Francisco', 'Anthony Jones', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Antonio José Manzanedo', 'Austin Hsu', 'Bastien L. Deharme', 'Bayard Wu', 'Ben Maier', 'Ben Wootten', 'Brandon Kitkouski', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Bryan Sola', 'Caio Monteiro', 'Campbell White', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Chase Stone', 'Chris Rahn', 'Chris Rallis', 'Chris Seaman', 'Christine Choi', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Craig J Spearing', 'Cristi Balanescu', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'Cyril Van Der Haegen', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Darek Zabrocki', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Allsop', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Gaillet', 'David Palumbo', 'David Rapoza', 'Deruchenko Alexander', 'Dimitar Marinski', 'Dmitry Burmak', 'Donato Giancola', 'Drew Baker', 'E. M. Gist', 'Ekaterina Burmak', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Erica Yang', 'Even Amundsen', 'Eytan Zana', 'Filip Burburan', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'G-host Lee', 'Gabor Szikszai', 'Greg Opalinski', 'Greg Staples', 'Grzegorz Rutkowski', 'Heather Hudson', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jack Wang', 'Jaime Jones', 'Jakub Kasper', 'Jama Jurabaev', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'Jana Schirmer & Johannes Voss', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Chan', 'Jason Felix', 'Jason Kang', 'Jason Rainville', 'Jasper Sandner', 'Jedd Chevrier', 'Jeff Easley', 'Jeff Simpson', 'Jehan Choo', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'Johan Grenier', 'Johann Bodin', 'Johannes Voss', 'John Avon', 'John Stanko', 'Jonas De Ro', 'Jonathan Kuo', 'Joseph Meehan', 'Josh Hass', 'Jung Park', 'Justin Sweet', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Karla Ortiz', 'Kev Walker', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Lake Hurwitz', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lie Setiawan', 'Lius Lasahido', 'Livia Prima', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Maciej Kuciara', 'Magali Villeneuve', 'Marco Nelor', 'Mark Behm', 'Mark Poole', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Winters', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Stewart', 'Matthew D. Wilson', 'Mauricio Calle', 'Micah Epstein', 'Michael Bruinsma', 'Michael Koelsch', 'Michael Komarck', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Mike Bierek', 'Mila Pesic', 'Milivoj Ćeran', 'Min Yum', 'Miranda Meeks', 'Mitchell Malloy', 'Nic Klein', 'Nils Hamm', 'Noah Bradley', 'Paolo Parente', 'Paolo Parente & Brian Snõddy', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Phill Simmer', 'Piotr Dura', 'Quinton Hoover', 'Ralph Horsley', 'Randy Vargas', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Ravenna Tran', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ron Spencer', 'Ryan Alexander Lee', 'Ryan Barger', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Ryan Yee', 'Sam Burley', 'Sam Wood', 'Sara Winters', 'Scott Chou', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Scott Murphy', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Shreya Shetty', 'Sidharth Chaturvedi', 'Simon Dominic', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Stephan Martiniere', 'Stephen Tappin', 'Steve Argyle', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Sung Choi', 'Suzanne Helmigh', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Tianhua X', 'Titus Lunter', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Trevor Claxton', 'Trevor Hairsine', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Tyler Walpole', 'Vance Kovacs', 'Victor Adame Minguez', 'Viktor Titov', 'Vincent Proce', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wayne England', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Wesley Burt', 'William Wu', 'Willian Murai', 'Winona Nelson', 'Wisnu Tan', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Yohann Schepacz', 'Yongjae Choi', 'Zack Stella', 'Zezhou Chen', 'Zoltan Boros', 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai', 'rk post']
